Q192295 | arts, technology | deccan | The Gol Gumbaz in Bijapur is a mausoleum of dark grey basalt holding the tomb of Mohammad Adil Shah, seventh ruler of the Bijapur Sultanate. Building halted in 1656, at his death. | The Gol Gumbaz in Bijapur is the huge domed tomb of a sultan. Work on it stopped when he died in 1656.
Q4022334 | arts, religion | pakistan | The Shah Jahan Mosque, or Friday Mosque of Thatta, is the main congregational mosque of the city of Thatta in Sindh. | The emperor Shah Jahan had a great mosque built in the city of Thatta in Sindh.
