Q646374 | power, trade | south | French India was a French colony of five separated enclaves that began as trading posts of the French East India Company: Pondichéry, Karikal, Yanaon, Mahé and Chandernagor. They joined India in 1950 and 1954. | France ruled five small pieces of land on the coasts of India, such as Pondicherry. They became part of India in the 1950s.
