Q1202492 | war, power | east | The Black Hole of Calcutta was a dungeon in Fort William, 14 by 18 feet, in which troops of Siraj-ud-Daulah, the Nawab of Bengal, held prisoners on the night of 20 June 1756. By one prisoner's account many died of suffocation. | In 1756 the Nawab of Bengal captured the British fort at Calcutta. Prisoners were locked overnight in a tiny cell, and many died.
Q203233 | war, power, trade | east | At the Battle of Plassey on 23 June 1757 the British East India Company under Robert Clive won a decisive victory over the Nawab of Bengal and his French allies. | In 1757 a British trading company defeated the ruler of Bengal at Plassey. It was the start of British rule in India.
